From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kim Hansen <github@kimhansen.dk>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:15:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Bounds-checked ByteReader; every response parser throws
 ResponseDecodingError instead of trapping

ByteReader's reads now check offset and count against the bytes actually
received and throw ResponseDecodingError.outOfBounds; Data.to(type:) uses
loadUnaligned, since a slice is rarely aligned for the type being read.
Message.Response.init(data:) and every response, file-information,
NTLM and DCERPC parser are now throwing, and Session/Connection propagate
the error to the caller instead of the process trapping on a truncated or
hostile reply. Wire counts that size an allocation (NetShareInfo1.count,
WStr.actualCount) and directory-entry offsets are checked against the
remaining bytes, and an unknown AV pair id is an error, not a force unwrap.
The generic read is constrained to FixedWidthInteger, which surfaced one
misread: FileFsVolumeInformation.SupportsObjects is a one-byte BOOLEAN,
but `reader.read() == 1` inferred Int and consumed eight bytes, shifting
the volume label. availableSpace multiplies in 64 bits and saturates.

RUMSKROT-HARDEN 1/5

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013Swhv8UXni3MZr9Kcar7wJ
